{"skill":{"slug":"mx-finance-search","displayName":"Financial Search Engine"},"version":{"version":"1.0.9","createdAt":1776424755002,"changelog":"Publish 1.0.9","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5072,"sha256":"60ccc1a2ff60b5f3905f51246c4f696d1695f95c56f45bdd5f623231e4d6cc0b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","size":12038,"sha256":"2d2655d4f1723989e029a4170b41a92e5ff95ccac925ac7d2b6d4b9a6490dad0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2150,"sha256":"026654bd62e2afeae641a9cd8f9d9a9db28cf01e47e3d06411b7593d26ebaa43","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789172718954,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1c5fd5d18cbf203960de906f542253266bc991eccde80a618afbdaacac2b08ac","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1c5fd5d18cbf203960de906f542253266bc991eccde80a618afbdaacac2b08ac","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085989098},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789172718954},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"medium","summary":"This skill is a disclosed financial search connector that uses a required Eastmoney API key and can save returned results locally by default.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill requires EM_API_KEY and sends it as an API header to the financial search service; this is purpose-aligned and disclosed, though users should treat the key as sensitive.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No package install, dependency fetch, tool replacement, startup hook, or installer-side mutation was found in the artifact files.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill description is broad and promotional, but the runtime behavior is narrow: one query, one remote search endpoint, optional stdout output, and default result-file saving.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Search results are written under a local miaoxiang/mx_finance_search directory by default, with a documented --no-save option; this is disclosed but may retain sensitive research queries or outputs.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is natural-language financial information search, and the implementation matches that core purpose by sending the user's query to an Eastmoney search endpoint and extracting response text.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving this skill an Eastmoney EM_API_KEY and sending financial research queries to the configured Eastmoney service. Use --no-save for sensitive searches, rotate or revoke the key if it is exposed, and avoid placing confidential client or regulated information in queries unless that service is approved for it.","findings":"[TT3] expected: The API key is read from EM_API_KEY and sent to the configured Eastmoney API endpoint for authentication, which is expected for this connector and disclosed in the skill documentation.\n[TP4] expected: The implementation is thinner than the broad description, but it still performs the advertised financial search function and discloses the provider and local-save behavior.\n[LP3] expected: Environment-variable use, outbound network access, and local result writing are visible in the artifact; the metadata only declares the environment variable, so clearer permission metadata would improve transparency.\n[SQP-1] expected: The activation wording is broad for financial research use cases, but the artifact does not show automatic background execution or unrelated access.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The script docstring says there are no environment reads, while the code immediately reads EM_API_KEY; the user-facing skill documentation correctly discloses the key requirement, so this is a documentation inconsistency rather than hidden behavior.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-language output and instructions are visible and consistent with the artifact's presentation; this is a usability/localization issue, not a security concern.\n[SDI-1] expected: Default local saving is real and should be considered before use, but it is documented and can be disabled with --no-save.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789172718954}}}}}